    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance that is visible from both directions of travel on the street.\n\n• Keep the driveway clear of parked vehicles to allow emergency vehicles to reach the residence without obstruction.\n\n• Mark any gate or fence entry points with reflective indicators so responders can locate access points quickly at night or in low-visibility conditions.\n\n• Keep at least one gate in the perimeter fencing unlocked or fitted with a breakaway lock to allow responders to reach the rear of the property on foot.\n\n• Trim any vegetation along the driveway that reduces vertical or side clearance for emergency vehicles.\n\n• Clear a level area near the residence where an ambulance or fire apparatus can stop and turn around, even if it requires repositioning stored items or vehicles during an emergency.\n\n• Mark the water feature with a visible indicator so responders moving on foot at night are aware of its location and can avoid it."
