    "recommendations": "• Trim branches from trees growing closest to the structure where vegetation is touching or within a few feet of the roofline or walls.\n\n• Thin the tree cluster nearest the structure to create open space between individual trees and between the trees and the building.\n\n• Remove shrubs growing directly against or immediately next to the structure.\n\n• Clear low-hanging branches from large trees near the structure so fire cannot climb from ground level into the tree canopy.\n\n• Keep the driveway clear of overhanging branches that could block vehicle access or drop burning material onto vehicles during an evacuation.\n\n• Thin vegetation growing along both sides of the driveway to maintain a clear travel path and improve visibility along the route.\n\n• Maintain the single access route free of debris, fallen branches, and encroaching vegetation at all times, as it is the only way in and out for residents and responders."
